Body:
I've submitted a PR (#39569) to fix this properly in the codebase. While waiting for it to be reviewed and merged, you can use the following **workaround** by configuring a custom OpenAI-compatible provider in your OpenCode config file (`~/.config/opencode/opencode.json` or project-level `.opencode.json`):

```json
{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",
  "provider": {
    "nvidia-glm": {
      "npm": "@ai-sdk/openai-compatible",
      "name": "NVIDIA NIM (GLM)",
      "options": {
        "baseURL": "https://integrate.api.nvidia.com/v1",
        "apiKey": "{env:NVIDIA_API_KEY}"
      },
      "models": {
        "z-ai/glm-5.2": {
          "name": "GLM 5.2 (thinking)",
          "interleaved": {
            "field": "reasoning_content"
          },
          "options": {
            "chat_template_kwargs": {
              "enable_thinking": true,
              "clear_thinking": false
            }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

Then select `nvidia-glm/z-ai/glm-5.2` from the model picker in OpenCode. Make sure to set the `NVIDIA_API_KEY` environment variable.

The key points:
- Uses `@ai-sdk/openai-compatible` instead of the built-in `nvidia` provider to avoid sending the unsupported `reasoningEffort` parameter.
- Injects `chat_template_kwargs` directly via `options`, which is what NVIDIA NIM expects for GLM models.
- Sets `interleaved.field` to `reasoning_content` so the thinking stream appears in the UI.

You can also verify the fix works by testing the raw API call with `curl`:

```bash
curl https://integrate.api.nvidia.com/v1/chat/completions \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $NVIDIA_API_KEY" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "model": "z-ai/glm-5.2",
    "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Prove sqrt(2) is irrational"}],
    "stream": true,
    "chat_template_kwargs": {"enable_thinking": true, "clear_thinking": false}
  }'
```

If you see `reasoning_content` in the stream, the workaround works correctly.

My PR (#39569) implements the same logic inside the built-in NVIDIA provider, so once merged, no manual configuration will be needed.
